Looking at the errors: `fflib_SObjects.IConstructor` doesn't exist (the inner `Constructor` is just a plain class the factory instantiates reflectively), `getSObjectType()`/`getType()` are virtual on `fflib_SObjects` and therefore need `override`, and the multi-line cast-then-chain expression in `construct(Set<Id>)` breaks the parser. I've rewritten that method as a simple cast onto a local (the same shape that already compiled elsewhere in the class) and kept the selector-factory injection so the factory can build the domain from record Ids.

